  "limits_note": "Joint limits in radians on the clip's Euler (Rz * Ry * Rx on the rest pose), checked on axis_probe sheets 2026-10-29: knee +X bends (never forward), elbow -X bends, foot +X points the toes down / -X lifts them (up to 40 degrees: a planted back foot in a deep stance), hand X bends the wrist forward/back, hand Y twists, hand Z bends it sideways (small), fingers: the curl axis differs between the plain rig v4 hands and the fingered (Mixamo-based) hands, so finger joints get one safe range on every axis (no finger joint past ~140 degrees: the user's own fist poses curl that far; thumbs ~80) until each rig's finger axes are probed. hinge: joints that only bend about X. Fight Studio's tools clamp to these; the Body Solve never turns a joint past them (a clip that already goes past keeps its own value, the solve just won't push further)."
